{% liquid
  assign faq_items = "What exactly are these chews made of?|4 simple ingredients: yak milk, cow milk, lime juice, and salt. That's the full list — no fillers, no preservatives, no artificial anything. It's the same recipe Himalayan families have used for centuries to make chhurpi (traditional hard cheese).||Where do they come from?|Our chews are handcrafted in Nepal using traditional methods, then packed in the USA before shipping to you. The yak and cow milk comes from free-grazing herds in the Himalayan foothills.||Are they actually natural?|Yes — and we mean it. 4 ingredients, all of which you can pronounce. No rawhide, no grain, no gluten, no artificial colors or flavors. What you see on the label is exactly what's inside.||How long do they last?|On average, about 67 minutes — but it depends on your dog's size and chewing style. Power chewers might go through one in 45 minutes; moderate chewers often get 90+ minutes. We have a size guide to help you pick the right match.||Do they smell bad or make a mess?|Barely! Unlike bully sticks or raw bones, yak chews have very little odor and don't leave greasy residue. Most families use them on the couch or carpet without issues. They're one of the cleanest long-lasting chews you'll find.||Are yak chews safe for my dog?|Yes, when sized correctly and supervised. Choose the right size for your dog's weight, always provide fresh water nearby, and take the chew away once it gets small enough to swallow whole. We also teach you how to turn that last nub into a safe, crunchy puff (the Nub Hack!).||Can they break my dog's teeth?|Yak chews are hard by design — that's what makes them last. Most healthy dogs do great with them. However, if your dog has dental issues, weak teeth, or tends to bite down with extreme force on their back molars, check with your vet first. We always recommend matching chew size to your dog's weight and style.||What's the thumbnail test?|It's a simple vet-recommended hardness check: press your thumbnail into the chew. If you can't make a small indent, it may be too hard for dogs with dental concerns. Our chews are intentionally dense (that's why they last!), so proper sizing and supervision matter most.||Are they safe for puppies?|For puppies over 6 months with their adult teeth coming in, yes — start with our Small size and supervise closely. For younger puppies still teething, we recommend waiting. Their baby teeth aren't built for hard chews yet.||What about senior dogs?|Many senior dogs love yak chews! But dental health matters most at this stage. If your senior has strong teeth and enjoys chewing, they'll likely do great. If they have dental disease or missing teeth, ask your vet first.||What if my dog swallows a piece?|Small pieces are generally digestible since they're made from cheese. But if your dog breaks off or swallows a large chunk, monitor them and contact your vet if you notice any distress. That's why we recommend removing the chew at about 2 inches — or use our Nub Hack to puff it into a safe treat.||How often can I give my dog a yak chew?|Most families offer one 3-5 times per week as part of an evening wind-down or during work calls. There's no strict limit, but like any treat, moderation is good. Fresh water should always be available.||How long do they actually last per session?|It depends on your dog! Light chewers might stretch one across multiple sessions. Power chewers average about 45-67 minutes. Our chew duration estimator can give you a better starting point based on your dog's breed and weight.||What's the Nub Hack?|When the chew gets down to about 2 inches, take it away from your dog. Soak it in water for 10 minutes, then microwave for 45-60 seconds. It puffs up into a crunchy, safe treat — like a bonus second chew! Let it cool completely before giving it back.||How do I choose the right size?|Match by weight: Small (under 20 lbs), Medium (20-50 lbs), Large (50-80 lbs), Extra Large (80+ lbs). When in between sizes, always go up — a slightly larger chew is safer than one that's too small. Our 30-second quiz can help.||How fast do orders ship?|Most orders ship within 1-2 business days and arrive in 3-5 business days via USPS or UPS. Free shipping on orders over $30.||What's your return policy?|We have a 30-day tail-wag guarantee. If your dog doesn't love it — or if you're not happy for any reason — reach out and we'll make it right. No hoops, no hassle.||Can I change or cancel my subscription?|Absolutely. Skip a month, change your delivery frequency, swap sizes, or cancel entirely — all from your account page. No hidden commitments, no penalty fees. We want you to stay because your dog loves it, not because you're locked in.||How does Subscribe and Save work?|Choose your chew size and how often you want it delivered (every 2, 4, 6, or 8 weeks). You'll get 20% off your first delivery and up to 30% off ongoing orders. Your dog never runs out, and you never have to remember to reorder.||Why is Prime different from other yak chews?|Three things: First, our founder actually grew up with this tradition in Nepal — this isn't a trend we jumped on. Second, we obsess over sizing and education so you pick the right chew the first time. Third, we stand behind every single chew with our 30-day guarantee. If your dog doesn't love it, we'll fix it." | split: "||"
%}

<section class="prime-faq-page" aria-labelledby="PrimeFaqTitle">
  <div class="pfq-shell">
    <header class="pfq-hero">
      <p class="pfq-kicker">Frequently asked questions</p>
      <h1 id="PrimeFaqTitle">Everything you need to know before your dog's first chew.</h1>
      <p>
        Real answers about safety, sizing, ingredients, and shipping — written by dog people,
        for dog people. No jargon, no runaround.
      </p>
      <div class="pfq-actions" aria-label="FAQ actions">
        <a href="/pages/how-long-will-this-last-for-my-dog" class="pfq-button pfq-button--primary">Find your dog's size</a>
        <a href="/pages/subscribe-and-save" class="pfq-button pfq-button--secondary">Never run out</a>
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="pfq-button pfq-button--secondary">Ask us anything</a>
      </div>
      <div class="pfq-search">
        <label for="PrimeFaqSearch">Search questions</label>
        <input id="PrimeFaqSearch" type="search" placeholder="Try: puppy, size, shipping, ingredients..." autocomplete="off">
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="pfq-layout">
      <aside class="pfq-sidebar" aria-label="FAQ categories">
        <a href="#product">Product</a>
        <a href="#safety">Safety</a>
        <a href="#duration">Duration</a>
        <a href="#sizing">Sizing</a>
        <a href="#orders">Orders</a>
        <a href="#subscriptions">Subscribe &amp; Save</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="pfq-content">
        <section class="pfq-category" id="product">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Product & ingredients</p>
          {% for item in faq_items limit: 5 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item" {% if forloop.first %}open{% endif %}>
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="safety">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Safety & digestion</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 5 limit: 8 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div>
                <p>{{ parts[1] }}</p>
                <p class="pfq-related">
                  {% case parts[0] %}
                    {% when 'Are yak chews safe for dogs?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Read the yak chew safety guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/how-long-will-this-last-for-my-dog">Use the size estimator</a>
                    {% when 'Are yak chews better than rawhide?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/best-rawhide-alternative">Compare rawhide alternatives</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/natural-dog-chews">Explore natural dog chews</a>
                    {% when 'Can puppies eat yak chews?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chews-for-puppies">Read the puppy yak chew guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Review safety basics</a>
                    {% when 'What if my dog swallows a small piece?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Read small-piece safety guidance</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/contact">Contact support</a>
                    {% when 'How often should I give a yak chew?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/are-yak-chews-digestible">Read the digestibility guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/how-long-do-yak-chews-last">Plan chew duration</a>
                    {% else %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Read the safety guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/collections/all">Shop by size</a>
                  {% endcase %}
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="duration">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Chew duration & routine</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 13 limit: 2 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="sizing">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Sizing & recommendations</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 15 limit: 1 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="orders">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Shipping & support</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 16 limit: 3 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="subscriptions">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Subscribe & Save</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 19 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pfq-support">
      <div>
        <p class="pfq-kicker">Still unsure?</p>
        <h2>We can help you choose.</h2>
        <p>Send your dog's breed, weight, age, and chewing style. Average response time is 4 business hours, Monday-Friday 9am-5pm CT.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/pages/contact" class="pfq-button pfq-button--primary">Ask a question</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {% for item in faq_items %}
      {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": {{ parts[0] | json }},
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": {{ parts[1] | strip_html | json }}
        }
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {% endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

<script>
  (function() {
    var input = document.getElementById('PrimeFaqSearch');
    if (!input) return;
    var items = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.pfq-item'));
    var categories = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.pfq-category'));

    input.addEventListener('input', function() {
      var query = input.value.trim().toLowerCase();
      items.forEach(function(item) {
        var text = item.textContent.toLowerCase();
        var match = !query || text.indexOf(query) !== -1;
        item.hidden = !match;
        if (match && query) item.open = true;
      });
      categories.forEach(function(category) {
        var visible = category.querySelector('.pfq-item:not([hidden])');
        category.hidden = !visible;
      });
    });

    items.forEach(function(item, index) {
      var answer = item.querySelector('div');
      if (!answer || answer.querySelector('.pfq-helpful')) return;

      var helpful = document.createElement('div');
      helpful.className = 'pfq-helpful';
      helpful.innerHTML = '<span>Was this helpful?</span><button type="button" data-helpful="yes">Yes</button><button type="button" data-helpful="no">No</button>';
      answer.appendChild(helpful);

      helpful.addEventListener('click', function(event) {
        var button = event.target.closest('button');
        if (!button) return;
        helpful.dataset.selected = button.dataset.helpful;
        helpful.setAttribute('aria-label', button.dataset.helpful === 'yes' ? 'Marked helpful' : 'Marked not helpful');
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

